SUMMARY:Econometrics – Ayden Higgins (University of Exeter) – Jackknife
  Inference for Fixed Effects Models
LOCATION:Room \, 
DESCRIPTION:Ayden Higgins: “Jackknife Inference for Fixed Effects Models
 ”\nhttps://ahiggins.co.uk/\n\nABSTRACT:\nThis paper develops a general m
 ethod of inference for fixed effects models which is (i) automatic\, (ii) 
 computationally inexpensive\, (iii) tuning parameter-free\, and (iv) highl
 y model agnostic. Specifically\, we show how to combine a collection of su
 bsample estimators into a jackknife $t$-statistic\, from which hypothesis 
 tests\, confidence intervals\, and $p$-values are readily obtained.
END:VEVENT
